========================================================================
Behavioural compatibility with other libraries
========================================================================

To reproduce the results of Warp 10, this product re-implements, from their
public specifications and by black-box comparison, the observable behaviour
of components it does not include and whose code it does not reuse: the
Java class library (java.lang.Math, java.util.Random, java.util.Formatter,
java.util.BitSet, Double.toString…; OpenJDK is GPLv2 with the Classpath
exception and no OpenJDK code is used), Joda-Time (Apache-2.0, "This
product includes software developed by Joda.org (https://www.joda.org/)"),
the Jackson JSON processor (Apache-2.0, originally written by Tatu
Saloranta) and Google Guava (Apache-2.0).
